From 0b114d471e50456bed6b78204584ef5d0e40b948 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kartikya Motwani <kartikya@local>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 04:36:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix missing logzero/websocket-client deps breaking Angel One
 feed at runtime

Deployed and tested PRICE_FEED=angel today - every symbol failed with
"No module named 'logzero'". smartapi-python's own package metadata
only declares requests, six, and python-dateutil as dependencies, but
its actual source (smartConnect.py, smartApiWebsocket.py) imports
logzero and websocket (websocket-client) directly - a packaging bug
on smartapi-python's end, not something pip could have caught
automatically from requirements.txt alone.

Verified by inspecting the installed wheel's METADATA and grep'ing its
source for the actual imports, then confirmed the fix by installing
fresh and running the full import chain (SmartApi, pyotp, our
angel_feed.py, AngelLiveFeed) plus actually instantiating SmartConnect
- all clean now, generateSession/ltpData both present as methods.

Added: logzero==1.7.0, websocket-client==1.8.0. All 17 tests still
pass. This was a dependency-resolution bug, unrelated to the Angel
One code itself - the AngelLiveFeed/angel_feed.py logic from the
earlier commit is unchanged.
---
 .gitignore       | 4 +++-
 requirements.txt | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/.gitignore b/.gitignore
index f99716c..9c3ea3d 100644
--- a/.gitignore
+++ b/.gitignore
@@ -3,4 +3,6 @@ __pycache__/
 *.pyc
 .env
 tradebot.db
-*.tar.gz
\ No newline at end of file
+*.tar.gz
+# logzero's default log output, created at runtime when SmartApi is used
+logs/
diff --git a/requirements.txt b/requirements.txt
index 1d736e4..931ec9d 100644
--- a/requirements.txt
+++ b/requirements.txt
@@ -4,6 +4,8 @@ sqlalchemy==2.0.35
 pydantic==2.9.2
 python-dotenv==1.0.1
 smartapi-python==1.4.8
+logzero==1.7.0
+websocket-client==1.8.0
 pyotp==2.9.0
 pandas>=2.2.3
 requests==2.32.3
-- 
2.43.0

